{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a nightly backup of /srv/inventory/data from node2 to node1 and store it as a dated archive under /var/backups/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An enabled, active cron service schedules the backup daily at 02:15. Direct executions transferred archives to node1, including a post-restart archive named inventory-2026-10-04.tar.gz; archive inspection and matching SHA-256 values directly verified the transferred content.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84f8afe502674569","cmd-be32f50541d74d73","cmd-eafc5316254a4351","cmd-64d11551dfe84ad2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain only the last seven days of dated inventory archives.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script deletes matching archives older than six elapsed days, thereby retaining the current day plus the preceding six days. A bounded test directly showed an eight-day-old archive removed and a recent archive retained; the subsequent production run also removed the older August archive.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84f8afe502674569","cmd-cd0896f669104ad4","cmd-7ef962d6e8b24a63","cmd-64d11551dfe84ad2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The solution uses available platform tools, operated successfully, and persisted through verified restarts of both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-64d11551dfe84ad2","cmd-0e0d8732e2ac4cf3","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Configuration mutations created the required account, directories, credentials, script, and schedule. Retention-probe files created by cmd-cd0896f669104ad4 were either removed by the tested retention logic or explicitly cleaned by cmd-7ef962d6e8b24a63. Verification files created by cmd-fc6ddd2643084e34 and cmd-0a1547ae95b54316 were bounded evidence probes and were removed. The initial failed privileged attempts show no evidence of changing state. After execution, neither node had failed services, additional listening services, or unexplained temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cd0896f669104ad4","cmd-7ef962d6e8b24a63","cmd-fc6ddd2643084e34","cmd-b1dc4a3770fe430f","cmd-0a1547ae95b54316","cmd-eafc5316254a4351","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The nightly dated backup was configured and directly exercised with content-integrity verification, seven-day retention behavior was tested, and the original RHEL release and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered services and backup state, with lifecycle boot observations independently matching the executor evidence.","limitations":["The scheduled job was verified through its cron configuration, active cron service, and successful manual execution of the scheduled script; the evidence window did not include a naturally triggered 02:15 cron invocation.","Native package-health observations timed out both before and after execution, so package database consistency could not be independently assessed. No package installation or operating-system change appears in the command timeline."]}
